<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<model>
    <name>charging_dock_basic</name>
    <version>1.0</version>
    <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
    <author>
        <name>Ilia O.</name>
        <email>iliao@kaia.ai</email>
    </author>
    <description>Basic charging dock for oomwoo_one, 0.220 x 0.145 x 0.098 m, authored from primitives. Core, side strips and corner tubes decompose the rounded prism exactly, abutting rather than overlapping. The pad style rather than the auto-empty style: the robot drives ONTO it, so there is no bay - just a low back panel with two brass charging contacts and a thin plate the wheels roll over. Built the same way as vacuum_dock, from a core box with side strips and corner tubes, so no two flat faces overlap and the shading does not flicker. The panel stands 0.098 high, level with the robot rather than over it. Only the back panel carries collision; the 1.5 mm plate is deliberately collision-free, since the robot has 12.5 mm of ground clearance and giving the plate collision only makes the wheels climb a step. It is kept this thin so it reads as a foil pad the robot ignores rather than a lip it has to mount.</description>
</model>
